{
  "description": "Input of extraction/generate_provenance.py. semantic = taxonomy {id, category}: id equals the section contract id (and the id in the sibling ia.json), category is one of the closed semanticCategories and is the single taxonomy of a section (it must equal the sibling ia.json category when that file is present). source = provenance of the implementing code {id, tag, file, lines, anchor}: derived from the contract's implementedBy (component name -> its definition in the real source file, range found by brace matching) plus the rendered root tag from extraction/measured-values.json sectionHeights; an explicit source override pins a narrower file/lines/anchor. retrievalIneligible lists the pinned sections that a retrieval layer must not return as an exemplar (layout-only utility and runtime UI), each with a reason of 30+ characters. Everything else is retrievable by default.",
  "semanticCategories": [
    "COLLECTION",
    "CONTENT",
    "CONVERSION",
    "DIVIDER",
    "FAQ",
    "FEATURE",
    "HERO",
